        "original_id": "3d9d71e3-7f65-5648-ab2b-1514507132eb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: North Hoyle Offshore Wind Farm, Liverpool Bay\n- Water bodies: Irish Sea\n- Transport: SS Ellan Vannin\n- Topics: offshore wind power, maritime loss\n\nFacts:\n- Liverpool Bay is a bay of the Irish Sea located between northeast Wales, Cheshire, Lancashire, and Merseyside on the eastern side of the Irish Sea.\n- On 3 December 1909, SS Ellan Vannin was lost in a storm in Liverpool Bay after serving under the name \"Ellan Vannin\" for a further 26 years.\n- North Hoyle Offshore Wind Farm is Wales' first offshore wind farm and the United Kingdom's first major offshore renewable power project.",
